In this paper, we propose a novel method for estimating both the bottleneck and available bandwidths with reasonable accuracy while minimizing network overhead by adopting machine learning. Our proposed method selects features of interest based on queueing theory for training machine learning models. Results from emulation experiments show that the model built with Extremely Randomized Trees (Extra Trees) algorithm achieves the best mean absolute percentage error (MAPE) of 28% and 26% for the bottleneck and available bandwidths, respectively.